package kgen

func init() {
	opsEntries = append(opsEntries, opsDoc{"ext:RingTemptsYou", "OpExt ExtRingTemptsYou (Obj the player)",
		"The Ring tempts the player Obj names, the resolving controller (gorge effRingTemptsYou: no corpus line carries Defined$; CR 701.54a). The seat's temptation count rises by one and a creature they control becomes (or stays) their Ring-bearer: none controlled counts and clears the designation (CR 701.54d), exactly one is designated silently (the strict-supersets rule), more than one asks the seat (the ring_bearer ask, gorge's KChoose) with the deterministic default -- the existing Ring-bearer when still controlled, else the first eligible creature in zone order -- offered first, and a stale or stray answer falls back to the default (gorge ringAnsweredBearer). Every path queues the \"Whenever the Ring tempts you\" listeners (TrigRingTemptsYou; gorge ringTemptsMatches: the event's player the tempted seat, its object the new bearer; with no bearer a ValidCard$ trigger never fires). While the seat has the emblem (the count is above zero, CR 701.54e) its abilities read live. The first (CR 701.54c): the Ring-bearer is legendary (typesGen adds Legendary, act_ring.go ringLegend) and can't be blocked by creatures with greater power (canBlock, ringOutpowers). The others are the emblem's triggered levels, queued after the event's card triggers, level N active when the count has reached N (gorge checkRingEmblemTriggers): level 2 when the Ring-bearer attacks, its controller draws a card then discards one (the dredge-aware draw site, the discard the player's own choice; act_ring.go ringAtkTrigs/resolveRingTrig); level 3 once per creature the Ring-bearer becomes blocked by, at resolution an end-of-combat promise registers to sacrifice that creature (its controller's; the queue-time incarnation stamp, CR 400.7; ringPromiseReg, fired at the end-of-combat step); level 4 when the Ring-bearer deals combat damage to a player, each opponent of its controller loses 3 life (ringCombatHit). Bilbo, Retired Burglar, Call of the Ring, Nazgûl. dirac/act_ring.go."})
}
